('Dehumidifiers','A Calmer Basement Starts With the Right Dehumidifier','A downstairs room can smell stale after a week of rain even when no leak is visible.','Measure the space, check drainage access, and choose a unit with an easy-to-clean filter.','A larger tank reduces emptying trips, but its weight matters if you carry it upstairs.','Aeocky'),
('Dehumidifiers','What to Look for in a Dehumidifier for a Small Apartment','A compact apartment may have one damp bedroom and very little floor space.','Prioritize a manageable footprint, noise information, and a tank you can remove without shifting furniture.','Tiny units are easier to place but may collect moisture more slowly.','Aeocky'),
